---
source: tests/cli_help.rs
expression: help_output(args)
---
Add a task. The text is its title, exactly as given

Usage: ms-todo tasks add [OPTIONS] <TEXT>

Arguments:
  <TEXT>  The task's title, taken literally

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>        Output format: jsonl is one object per line, ids one ID per line, csv has a header row [default: table in a terminal, json when piped] [possible values: table, json, jsonl, ids, csv]
      --list <NAME|ID>         The list's exact name or its ID [default: the "Tasks" list]
      --due <WHEN>             Due date: 2026-10-02, today, tomorrow, fri, next mon, in 3 days, +2w, 12 oct, 12/10 (day first), end of month. Due dates have no time; put a time in --reminder
      --instance <NAME>        Use a separate copy of ms-todo's data (also MS_TODO_INSTANCE). Builds run from Cargo's target/ directory default to "dev"; "default" is the installed copy
      --reminder <WHEN>        Remind me at this local time: 17:30 (the next one), tomorrow 9am, fri 5:30pm, 2026-10-02 09:30. A day alone, such as tomorrow or in 2 days, is 09:00 on it
      --importance <LEVEL>     How important it is: 1 or p1 (high), 2, 3, p2 or p3 (normal), 4 or p4 (low), or high, normal or low
      --body <TEXT>            Notes, as plain text
      --dry-run                Show what would be sent without changing anything
      --idempotency-key <KEY>  Run this change at most once: repeating the command with the same key returns the first result for 24 hours, and the same key with a different change exits 2
  -h, --help                   Print help
  -V, --version                Print version
